  offerDialogue:
    name: Mills
    sentences:
    - "Here's the project."
    - "Build a crossing that gives worker buses a direct route into the industrial district."
    - "We'll use a <b><#E09500>Bus</color></b> to test it. Your design must meet the site's requirements and carry it safely across."
    - "Consider the span, supports, materials, and how loads travel through the structure."
    - "I won't give you a layout to follow. <b><#E09500>Use what you've learned, build your design, and let the results guide any changes</color></b>."
    - "You've handled many different projects, {PlayerName}. I'm looking forward to seeing how you put everything together. If you're ready, take the contract."
  continueOfferDialogue:
    name: Mills
    sentences: []
  reminderDialogue:
    name: Mills
    sentences:
    - "You've got the requirements and the experience to work through this one."
    - "<b><#E09500>Trust your reasoning and use the test results carefully</color></b> if something needs to change."
  finishedContractDialogue:
    name: Mills
    sentences:
    - "The buses have their own crossing now. That should make the journey into the industrial district easier and reduce traffic on the busiest freight roads."
    - "You had to consider how the whole bridge responds to the load, rather than focusing on a single concept."
    - "That's an important step, {PlayerName}. The final project will ask you to apply that same judgment to a much larger connection."
    - "First, let's review what you've put into practice here. There's one last site I'd like you to see afterward."
